  "proposal_scope": "Jointly draw a fresh hypothetical RunSeed and complete independent native act/map oracle prefix; retain only a prefix satisfying the public act, necessary second-route type and observed WingedBoots charge certificate. No source seed, source graph or trial map object is supplied to native replay.",
  "alias_and_stopping_law": "All repeated full pre-draw states within a trial reuse one word. Every clean nonmatch is a completed native trial; native errors and cancellation stop with partial accounting. With clean-miss probability b and fixed K, successful subdensity is p(prefix) 1[event] sum(b^j,j=0..K-1). This multiplier depends only on the fixed public root, so its reciprocal cancels with the same global envelope. If every trial completes, b=1-Z and p/q=Z/(1-(1-Z)^K). No numeric estimate of Z or claim that p/q equals one is used. Holding a latent RunSeed/history while retrying maps was explicitly rejected because its normalization may vary.",
  "replay_guards": "Ordered act/map trace and full aliases replay during ordinary native construction. The selected RunSeed, construction phase, map RNG address and RunState owner are checked. Later proposals cannot overwrite visited cells. Exact public packet equality remains the acceptance gate.",
  "failure_accounting": "Completed scratch trials, total words/distinct cells, selected trace, auxiliary and selected recipes, and RunSeed draws are distinct. Component budget exhaustion is computationally inconclusive, preserving all requested candidate mass and masks.",
